        "titolo_orig": "France resumes genocide probe against Rwanda ex-president's widow",
        "testo_it": "Francia: riaperta l'indagine sul genocidio in Ruanda contro la vedova dell'ex presidente.",
        "priorita": "Media",
        "id_gruppo": 11,
        "link": "https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260507-france-resumes-genocide-probe-against-rwanda-ex-president-s-widow",
        "orario": "12:14",
        "timestamp": 1778148895,
        "contenuto_esteso": "To display this content from YouTube, you must enable advertisement tracking and audience measurement. One of your browser extensions seems to be blocking the video player from loading. To watch this content, you may need to disable it on this site. France resumes genocide probe against Rwanda ex-president's widow Issued on: 07/05/2026 - 12:14 France's judiciary on Wednesday ordered the resumption of an almost two-decade investigation into accusations that the widow of Rwanda's former president Juvenal Habyarimana was involved in the 1994 genocide. Investigating magistrates last year dismissed the case into alleged complicity in genocide and crimes against humanity against Agathe Habyarimana over \"insufficient evidence\". But the judiciary overturned that decision and ordered that the investigation, which started in France in 2007, should continue. Burkina Faso junta secretly detained journalist and others, advocacy group says 07/05/2026 Rubio faces challenge in Pope Leo meeting after Trump's criticism over Iran 07/05/2026 US Rubio seeks to ease tensions with US pope after Trump's attacks 07/05/2026 Trump sees swift end to war as Iran reviews US peace proposal 07/05/2026 UK voters cast ballots in elections expected to deal blow to Starmer 07/05/2026 What to know about hantavirus, the illness linked to a cruise ship outbreak 07/05/2026 Argentina probes link to deadly hantavirus outbreak on Atlantic cruise 07/05/2026 Holders PSG edge Bayern Munich to reach Champions League final 07/05/2026 Cruise ship with hantavirus outbreak heads to Spain's Canary Islands after 3 are evacuated 07/05/2026"
